      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The transoral approach to the upper cervical spine is now well established. Oropharyngeal complications have not previously been critically assessed. In the present study, the overall complication rate was 31.6%. This dropped to 15.4% in those patients who did not undergo splitting of the soft palate. The complication rate of 75% in the split soft palate group means that this procedure should be discontinued where it is not absolutely necessary."},
